0,Cantares Mexicanos - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantares_Mexicanos,"April 10, 2026 - The Cantares Mexicanos is a manuscript collection of Nahuatl songs or poems recorded in the 16th century. The 91 songs of the Cantares form the largest Nahuatl song collection, containing over half of all known traditional Nahuatl songs. It is currently located in the National Library of Mexico ...","Nahuatl, Central Puebla",Uto-Aztecan
1,Central Puebla Nahuatl - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Puebla_Nahuatl,"February 15, 2025 - The Central Puebla Nahuatl language is a Nahuan language spoken by 16,000 people in Mexico with 1,430 monolinguals. It is also known as Central Puebla Aztec, Náhuatl del Suroeste de Puebla, and Southwestern Puebla Nahuatl.","Nahuatl, Central Puebla",Uto-Aztecan
