6,"Nahuatl, Northern Puebla",https://accentnetwork.com/nahuatl-northern-puebla/,"April 22, 2025 - Northern Puebla Nahuatl, spoken by around 40,000 people in Mexico, is part of the Uto-Aztecan language family. It is culturally significant in the northern Puebla region. Radio and local storytelling are popular, with mobile content increasingly accessed by younger speakers. Respect for elders is central...","Nahuatl, Central Puebla",Uto-Aztecan
